    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0562" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg490"/>

                <head>No. 299.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Stevens</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 125.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your dispatch No. 125, of
                    the 17th ultimo, relating to two cases in which the naturalization was disputed,
                    by the Swedish <pb facs="0563" n="491" xml:id="pg491"/> authorities, of one C.
                    M. Cedergren and one Peder Sigbjornsen, Skoland.</p>
                <p>Your action, as reported in the said dispatch, is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
